ents{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/timurproko","id":80062439,"login":"timurproko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMDYyNDM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timurproko","user_view_type":"public"}},"body":"## Proposal\n\nAdd a minimal, versioned fleet status view so Herdr avoids decoding full task history without losing old tasks whose pull requests remain open. Persist PR lifecycle facts, expire old merged or closed PRs, and exclude authoritatively missing PRs through narrowly bounded closed-task verification while preserving legacy status output.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- [x] Saved PR observations preserve lifecycle facts without granting delivery authority.\n- [x] Minimal fleet status bounds history by PR lifetime while preserving legacy output.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Fleet v1 emits only home, owner terminal/live, task identity and PR discovery fields with both version markers.\n- Every non-closed task remains visible; closed tasks retain open or unknown PRs, expire after 24 hours beyond a known merge or close, and exclude proven missing PRs immediately without rewriting URLs.\n- Discovery and replacement land/finish reads save identity-scoped facts without granting delivery authority; ambiguous 404, permission, authentication, rate-limit or transport failures never prove absence.\n- Only fleet discovery verifies closed recorded PRs, adding at most five requests inside the existing serial two-second subprocess and ten-second shared budget, with open refreshes at least ten minutes apart.\n- Observation saves yield to lifecycle work; supported atomic-write contention no longer causes internal-error exit 70 and exhausted locks return retryable task-busy refusals.\n- Legacy status output remains byte-compatible; unknown views exit with a stable diagnostic and help advertises the fleet capability.\n- Metadata-validated summaries avoid historical prose and copy inspection; a 1000-task history produces 364 bytes and indexed 5000-task polling stays well under one second locally.\n\n## Automation\n\n<details>\n<summary>Used by CI to link this PR to its OpenSpec change</summary>\n\n```openspec-implementation\n{\n  \"version\": 3,\n  \"change\": \"status-fleet-view\",\n  \"archive\": \"openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-24-status-fleet-view/\",\n  \"acceptanceManifest\": \"openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-24-status-fleet-view/acceptance.md\",\n  \"finalizedHead\": \"11e8c5460eccb58907a9875ce3ec22b0b9e1a2b8\"\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n","closed_at":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/issues/11/comments","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/pulls/11/commits","created_at":"2026-11-24T15:40:13Z","diff_url":"https://github.com/timurproko/crew/pull/11.diff","draft":false,"head":{"label":"timurproko:feature/status-fleet-view","ref":"feature/status-fleet-view","repo":{"allow_forking":true,"archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/{archive_format}{/ref}","archived":false,"assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/assignees{/user}","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/git/blobs{/sha}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/branches{/branch}","clone_url":"https://github.com/timurproko/crew.git","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/timurproko/crew/collaborators{/collaborator}","comment